    {
      "id": 146134,
      "name": "Ronway",
      "username": "Ronway",
      "avatar_template": "/user_avatar/forums.greaterthangames.com/ronway/{size}/1856_2.png",
      "created_at": "2015-08-12T03:53:00.000Z",
      "cooked": "<p>Spmething we know about whenever a card is destroyed, any destruction effect may still happen. Take Savage Mana versus Omnitron, if Haka does the killing blow to Omnitron, then you have the option to place him under Savage Mana, but Omnitron will still leave the game afterwards. If you choose to have Omnitron removed from the game first, he is no longer in the game to put under Savage Mana.</p><p>This is similar to Prime Warden Captain Cosmic's power, thanks to the \"instead\" on it. If it is first put under Savage Mana, you can totally shuffle it into PW Captain Cosmic's deck. However, if you choose to shuffle it first, then the \"instead\" would mean it wasn't actually destroyed, thus Savage Mana cannot trigger.</p>",
      "post_number": 5,
      "post_type": 1,
      "updated_at": "2021-02-07T04:24:01.122Z",
      "reply_count": 0,
      "reply_to_post_number": null,
      "quote_count": 0,
      "incoming_link_count": 0,
      "reads": 1,
      "readers_count": 0,
      "score": 0.2,
      "yours": false,
      "topic_id": 13414,
      "topic_slug": "savage-mana-and-prime-warden-captain-cosmics-base-power",
      "display_username": "Ronway",
      "primary_group_name": "playtesters",
      "flair_name": "playtesters",
      "flair_url": "/uploads/default/original/1X/f46928191dbf93b4d0df24571543f49779579225.png",
