    {
      "id": 146137,
      "name": "dwetuski",
      "username": "dwetuski",
      "avatar_template": "/letter_avatar_proxy/v4/letter/d/3e96dc/{size}.png",
      "created_at": "2016-10-28T18:20:09.000Z",
      "cooked": "<p>According to the text of Prime Wardens Captain Cosmic, the timing worksheet is wrong. &nbsp;Step 17 applies to cards that say \"would be destroyed\" (like Unforgiving Wasteland), indicating that the effect replaces the destruction. &nbsp;Cards that say \"is destroyed\" (like PWCC) respond to the destruction rather than replace it, and are handled by step 18. &nbsp;It could be that PWCC is <em>intended</em>&nbsp;to be a replacement effect but was worded as a response effect, in which case the text should be changed from \"is\" to \"would be\" (this has happened before).</p>",
      "post_number": 8,
      "post_type": 1,
      "updated_at": "2021-02-07T04:24:01.340Z",
      "reply_count": 0,
      "reply_to_post_number": null,
      "quote_count": 0,
      "incoming_link_count": 1,
      "reads": 1,
      "readers_count": 0,
      "score": 5.2,
